# Testing

Apply this rule when working in test files and whenever tests are added or changed.

- Mirror `frontend/` vs `backend/` separation. Do not mix UI and Lambda tests in one suite.
- Prefer small unit tests for `amountMinor` arithmetic, `userId` scoping, and the auth-adapter boundary.
- When touching SAM, LocalStack, or Docker paths, add or run local smoke checks against those services. Do not hit real AWS.
- Do not add paid CI or cloud test services unless explicitly asked.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
expect(total).toBeCloseTo(19.99);
await repo.listInvoices(); // no userId

// ✅ GOOD
expect(totalMinor).toBe(1999);
await expect(repo.listInvoices({ userId })).resolves.toEqual(
  expect.arrayContaining([expect.objectContaining({ userId })]),
);
```
